      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "971306174d1fe9cbca6634004418601c",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"branching-ratio-and-cascade-size-on-networks\">Branching ratio and cascade size on networks</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Replication notebook for the cascade paper. It compares four\ncombinations of degree (topology) and threshold heterogeneity, then\ngeneralizes both to the beta and beta-binomial families.</span>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Heterogeneous threshold</th>\n<th>Homogeneous threshold</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Het. topology</strong></td>\n<td>power-law x Pareto</td>\n<td>power-law x Gaussian</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Hom. topology</strong></td>\n<td>Poisson x Pareto</td>\n<td>Poisson x Gaussian</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ul>\n<li>Topology is the degree distribution; the threshold is the activation\n  threshold distribution.</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
